<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea sees rising cases of unfair stock trading.</title>
<headline>S.Korea sees rising cases of unfair stock trading.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea identified 143 cases of unfair stock trading for investigation in the year to June 30, up from 76 cases a year earlier, the Securities Supervisory Board (SSB) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of the total, 12 were cases of insider trading, up from three cases a year ago, and 17 were cases of stock price manipulation, down from 32, the board said.</p>
<p>Other unfair trading cases included cancellation of public announcements and dissemination of false rumours.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
